WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.167
-Seth Rogen's right.
The name actually is --

00:00:03.167 --> 00:00:04.834
It is weird not hearing
Machine Gun Kelly.

00:00:04.834 --> 00:00:06.901
-Yeah, is it odd now,
because you've become so famous

00:00:06.901 --> 00:00:09.734
as Machine Gun,
that you're not Colson anymore?

00:00:09.734 --> 00:00:11.968
-I was never -- I haven't been
Colson since I was 15.

00:00:11.968 --> 00:00:14.267
Since I was 15 years old, I was
like, "I'm Machine Gun Kelly."

00:00:14.267 --> 00:00:18.167
-Yeah. But Colson is just better
for when you're in movies?

00:00:18.167 --> 00:00:21.000
-You know, Nickelodeon and
Disney don't like Machine Gun.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.534
-Yeah, that makes sense.
That makes a lot of sense.

00:00:24.534 --> 00:00:26.000
It's your first time
in the chair.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:27.200
I'm so happy.
You've been here and performed.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:28.501
-Yeah.

00:00:28.501 --> 00:00:30.667
-By the way, I loved your --
I love your new album.

00:00:30.667 --> 00:00:32.534
-Thank you. Thank you.
-It's fantastic.

00:00:32.534 --> 00:00:35.934
Congratulations on it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:35.934 --> 00:00:37.701
But I'm happy
that you're actually here

00:00:37.701 --> 00:00:40.033
and sitting in the chair
and I get talk to you,

00:00:40.033 --> 00:00:41.834
because, man,
you're really fun to talk to.

00:00:41.834 --> 00:00:43.067
-Thanks.

00:00:43.067 --> 00:00:45.234
-Talking with you backstage,
I mean, we have --

00:00:45.234 --> 00:00:47.133
-I whispered something to you
one time when I performed here.

00:00:47.133 --> 00:00:49.868
I was, like, "Dude, I love that
song 'Snowball Fight!'"

00:00:49.868 --> 00:00:50.901
-I mean --

00:00:50.901 --> 00:00:52.667
-Which was -- Jimmy had an album

00:00:52.667 --> 00:00:54.667
I listened to a lot
in middle school.

00:00:54.667 --> 00:00:56.100
It's --

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:58.801
-I probably didn't even believe
that you said that to me.

00:00:58.801 --> 00:01:00.133
-If we replay it back,

00:01:00.133 --> 00:01:01.834
you'll probably see me just slip
it to you and walk away.

00:01:01.834 --> 00:01:03.033
But I was just like,
"Dude, I love that."

00:01:03.033 --> 00:01:05.400
-"Snowball Fight!" --
I mean, that was, like --

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:06.868
-♪ Snowball, snowball ♪

00:01:06.868 --> 00:01:09.133
♪ Snowball fight ♪

00:01:09.133 --> 00:01:12.334
-Yeah, please -- No, really,
everyone loves that.

00:01:12.334 --> 00:01:15.801
Please don't -- Please sit down.

00:01:15.801 --> 00:01:18.234
-We'll add applause
later in post.

00:01:18.234 --> 00:01:22.467
We both worked with
Cameron Crowe, which is cool.

00:01:22.467 --> 00:01:24.234
How much do you love
Cameron Crowe?

00:01:24.234 --> 00:01:26.400
-I love him so much that I
sent him a mean text.

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:27.467
-No.
-Yeah.

00:01:27.467 --> 00:01:28.467
-To Cameron Crowe,

00:01:28.467 --> 00:01:29.467
the nicest human?

00:01:29.467 --> 00:01:30.734
-The nicest human.

00:01:30.734 --> 00:01:33.834
The guy who actually
re-introduced me to my name.

00:01:33.834 --> 00:01:34.901
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:01:34.901 --> 00:01:36.000
-Because of "Roadies"?

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:38.534
-Yeah, when I did
that show, "Roadies,"

00:01:38.534 --> 00:01:39.934
I had a parking spot,
and it said "Colson."

00:01:39.934 --> 00:01:41.968
And I, like, walked around, and,
all the guys, you know,

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:43.901
it would be like,
"Bob," and "Jimmy,"

00:01:43.901 --> 00:01:45.334
and they'd be like,
"Hey, Colson," and whatever.

00:01:45.334 --> 00:01:49.801
And I was like, "Man, I think
I like my real name again."

00:01:49.801 --> 00:01:52.501
-That was Cameron that did that?
And you sent him a mean text?

00:01:52.501 --> 00:01:55.000
-So, I have this thing
in my life where

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:57.501
I just, like, run everyone
away that loves me.

00:01:57.501 --> 00:02:00.067
And, so, Cameron loves me,
and I have this thing where

00:02:00.067 --> 00:02:02.367
I was like,
"You can't love me too much,

00:02:02.367 --> 00:02:04.200
'cause I'm gonna run you away."

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:05.534
-Like a snap.

00:02:05.534 --> 00:02:08.000
-So, I would
always call Cameron,

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:09.000
and he would always answer

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:10.767
and he would kind of just,
you know,

00:02:10.767 --> 00:02:12.734
give me advice or,
you know, whatever.

00:02:12.734 --> 00:02:13.767
And, so,
he didn't answer my call.

00:02:13.767 --> 00:02:15.100
I think I called him
like three times,

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:16.534
you know, over a period of
like three days.

00:02:16.534 --> 00:02:17.734
Called him three times,
he didn't answer.

00:02:17.734 --> 00:02:19.100
And I texted him and I said,

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:22.200
"Oh, it's so punk rock
that you don't answer."

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:23.968
-Yeah.
-He never answered that.

00:02:23.968 --> 00:02:25.868
-He never answered?!
That's even more punk rock!

00:02:25.868 --> 00:02:28.767
-It's so punk rock. I know.
-It's even more.

00:02:28.767 --> 00:02:29.901
Well, Cameron,
if you're watching,

00:02:29.901 --> 00:02:31.033
we both love you.

00:02:31.033 --> 00:02:32.434
-To be fair,
I sent him a follow-up text,

00:02:32.434 --> 00:02:34.400
and I was like, "In case you
didn't get my humor,

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:38.100
I was just..."

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:41.033
-You do have a good sense of
humor, I will say.

00:02:41.033 --> 00:02:43.334
Pete Davidson
was on our show recently,

00:02:43.334 --> 00:02:45.534
and we talked about
you guys getting together.

00:02:45.534 --> 00:02:48.701
And you fell off the stage
together at good-nights

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:50.067
at "Saturday Night Live."

00:02:50.067 --> 00:02:51.634
-If you show that clip,
I am gonna...

00:02:51.634 --> 00:02:53.100
-I would never.
Can we show --

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:55.267
-Oh, God. Okay.
[ Drumroll ]

00:02:55.267 --> 00:02:57.501
-There you go. Watch this.
-Oh, God! Oh, no!

00:02:57.501 --> 00:02:59.734
-Whoa!

00:02:59.734 --> 00:03:02.300
-So, then -- So, I --

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:07.634
So, I go to Pete --
I go, "What happened?

00:03:07.634 --> 00:03:09.667
What was that thing?
What happened with Machine Gun?"

00:03:09.667 --> 00:03:13.534
And he goes,
"He had a bruised coccyx."

00:03:13.534 --> 00:03:14.634
And I go, "What?"

00:03:14.634 --> 00:03:16.801
He goes,
"He bruised his coccyx."

00:03:16.801 --> 00:03:17.934
-It was bad.

00:03:17.934 --> 00:03:19.200
-No, but I don't even know
what a coccyx is.

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:20.567
-I didn't know
what it was either

00:03:20.567 --> 00:03:23.100
until the doctor was like,
"Well, you bruised your coccyx."

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:24.567
-Wait. Alright, so --

00:03:24.567 --> 00:03:29.234
-Like three different X-rays
over in three different states.

00:03:29.234 --> 00:03:30.434
I was like, "What's going --

00:03:30.434 --> 00:03:32.934
Why can't I sit or stand
or do anything?"

00:03:32.934 --> 00:03:36.467
They were like, "You see this
area here in your ass?

00:03:36.467 --> 00:03:37.801
It's...

00:03:37.801 --> 00:03:40.734
-Alright, so that's a coccyx.
-Yeah, it's your butt.

00:03:40.734 --> 00:03:44.234
-How did you go about
bruising your coccyx?

00:03:44.234 --> 00:03:50.667
-I was -- I had a match with
Post Malone in a beer-pong game.

00:03:50.667 --> 00:03:53.801
And --
-As one does. Yeah, okay.

00:03:53.801 --> 00:03:55.734
I think I've played beer pong
against Post Malone.

00:03:55.734 --> 00:03:57.434
-And you know when you get
the cup and you start drinking?

00:03:57.434 --> 00:03:58.467
-Of course.

00:03:58.467 --> 00:03:59.467
-So, we didn't even
get to the game,

00:03:59.467 --> 00:04:00.534
and I started drinking.

00:04:00.534 --> 00:04:02.968
And, so,
they filmed on the way out.

00:04:02.968 --> 00:04:05.000
They did, like, a "Rocky,"
like, boxing match,

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:06.467
like, you know,
film on the way out.

00:04:06.467 --> 00:04:08.033
And I, like, couldn't take
the pressure of the camera,

00:04:08.033 --> 00:04:10.234
so I was like, "Alright,
every five steps,

00:04:10.234 --> 00:04:12.767
I got to do something cool,
'cause it's like 500 steps.

00:04:12.767 --> 00:04:14.601
I don't just want to just walk."

00:04:14.601 --> 00:04:16.267
So I was like,
"Got to do something.

00:04:16.267 --> 00:04:18.067
So every five steps,
I'd be like...

00:04:18.067 --> 00:04:20.267
And then there
was a staircase rail,

00:04:20.267 --> 00:04:21.567
and I was like, "Yeah, great."

00:04:21.567 --> 00:04:24.734
So I'd hit the staircase rail
and I rode it down.

00:04:24.734 --> 00:04:27.934
At the bottom of it,
I didn't see a giant spike,

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:31.734
and it just, you know...

00:04:31.734 --> 00:04:34.067
-Bruised your coccyx.
-Yeah, it rammed...

00:04:34.067 --> 00:04:37.667
[ Laughter ]
-Wow! Talk about --

00:04:37.667 --> 00:04:39.367
-It did something
that was not --

00:04:39.367 --> 00:04:41.501
-Yeah. Did you play it off?

00:04:41.501 --> 00:04:42.567
-I -- I -- I --

00:04:42.567 --> 00:04:43.567
-You played it off like
it was cool?

00:04:43.567 --> 00:04:44.801
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:44.801 --> 00:04:47.367
And then this was also,
like, right when I was

00:04:47.367 --> 00:04:49.400
starting to date,
you know, Megan.

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:53.267
And I, like --
I was holding it together.

00:04:53.267 --> 00:04:54.801
It was just --
It was a bad night.

00:04:54.801 --> 00:04:57.367
Like, the whole --
Like, I won the Ping-Pong match.

00:04:57.367 --> 00:04:58.834
I went home.

00:04:58.834 --> 00:05:01.534
I was like -- I had this --
Travis got me this --

00:05:01.534 --> 00:05:03.567
He got me a knife that was --

00:05:03.567 --> 00:05:05.234
that had an engravement from
the new album on it.

00:05:05.234 --> 00:05:06.234
And I was like,
"Oh, check this out.

00:05:06.234 --> 00:05:07.567
This is sick."

00:05:07.567 --> 00:05:09.067
And I threw it up, and it came
and stuck in my hand.

00:05:09.067 --> 00:05:10.868
Do you see that right here?
-I do see that.

00:05:10.868 --> 00:05:12.734
-Yeah, that was from when
a knife stuck in my --

00:05:12.734 --> 00:05:13.734
'Cause you know how
you throw it up

00:05:13.734 --> 00:05:14.968
and you're supposed to catch it?

00:05:14.968 --> 00:05:17.267
I looked at her and I was like,
"Check this out."

00:05:17.267 --> 00:05:18.300
And I was like, "Ugggh!"

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:20.367
-She's like, "You are

00:05:20.367 --> 00:05:22.000
the coolest dude
I've ever met in my life.

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:23.000
Kiss me!"

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:24.267
Wow!

00:05:24.267 --> 00:05:25.400
-And then, the next morning,
as soon as she left,

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:28.734
I was like, "Yo,
I need stitches real quick."

00:05:28.734 --> 00:05:30.033
-Yeah, like, "Dude, I got a
bruised coccyx over here

00:05:30.033 --> 00:05:31.133
and a knife in my hand."

00:05:31.133 --> 00:05:34.033
-A bruised coccyx
and a knife in my hand.

00:05:34.033 --> 00:05:35.234
-Dude, that's so --

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:36.300
-Yeah, and so
I didn't have strength,

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:37.534
so when I picked Pete --

00:05:37.534 --> 00:05:40.934
And, like, Pete is a --
He's a method person.

00:05:40.934 --> 00:05:44.400
Like, he's always a different
shape every time I see him.

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:45.734
-Yeah, he is a little --
-He is.

00:05:45.734 --> 00:05:48.434
He has different hair,
different -- He's like, "Dude,

00:05:48.434 --> 00:05:50.234
I just worked out for
two months straight.

00:05:50.234 --> 00:05:52.267
-Then he's
super-skinny and tall.

00:05:52.267 --> 00:05:53.434
-Yeah. And, so, this time,
he was, like --

00:05:53.434 --> 00:05:54.601
I showed up,
and he was sweating.

00:05:54.601 --> 00:05:56.367
He was like, "What's up, bro?
What's up?"

00:05:56.367 --> 00:05:58.234
He was huge, and I was like,
"Yeah, like, we should do

00:05:58.234 --> 00:05:59.234
something funny."

00:05:59.234 --> 00:06:01.400
And then, like, you know, he --

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:04.100
-Well, you're both tall dudes.
How tall are you?

00:06:04.100 --> 00:06:06.667
-6'4".
-Yeah, that's tall.

00:06:06.667 --> 00:06:07.801
And Pete's tall.
-Yeah.

00:06:07.801 --> 00:06:09.634
-So to lift up a tall man --
that's --

00:06:09.634 --> 00:06:10.634
And you're tall.

00:06:10.634 --> 00:06:11.934
That's a big fall.

00:06:11.934 --> 00:06:13.300
-I was -- You know what?

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:15.834
I think I was -- Subconsciously,
I think I let myself --

00:06:15.834 --> 00:06:19.567
I was like, "'SNL,' how did you
not do a sketch with us?"

00:06:19.567 --> 00:06:22.167
And I was like,
"30 seconds left to go.

00:06:22.167 --> 00:06:24.467
I'll come up with something."

00:06:24.467 --> 00:06:25.701
-Here's a sketch.

00:06:25.701 --> 00:06:27.167
By the way, you crushed
that performance.

00:06:27.167 --> 00:06:29.100
Both performances, by the way,
were fantastic.

00:06:29.100 --> 00:06:31.300
-Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:34.434
-I loved that you did something
different, and it was cool.

00:06:34.434 --> 00:06:37.934
I want to talk about your movie.
This is "The Last Son."

00:06:37.934 --> 00:06:39.334
Congrats on this.

00:06:39.334 --> 00:06:41.801
You got to do something that
I am actually so jealous of.

00:06:41.801 --> 00:06:43.901
You got to kick open
a saloon door.

00:06:43.901 --> 00:06:45.234
-Over and over again.

00:06:45.234 --> 00:06:46.634
But it wasn't --
It was never in the movie.

00:06:46.634 --> 00:06:49.200
It was just off camera.
-No, it doesn't matter.

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:52.367
-We lived on set,
so I lived in the barbershop,

00:06:52.367 --> 00:06:55.634
which was adjacent
from the saloon,

00:06:55.634 --> 00:06:56.968
which held all the wardrobe.

00:06:56.968 --> 00:07:01.734
Like, all the shots in
the movie are in this town.

00:07:01.734 --> 00:07:04.667
It was beautifully shot,
but, like, you know,

00:07:04.667 --> 00:07:07.501
there was always --
All the cast lived on there,

00:07:07.501 --> 00:07:08.901
except for, like,
Sam Worthington.

00:07:08.901 --> 00:07:10.934
I think he was method and, like,
lived in the woods or something.

00:07:10.934 --> 00:07:12.067
-Wow!

00:07:12.067 --> 00:07:13.634
-'Cause I never saw him
in the town,

00:07:13.634 --> 00:07:15.100
except for when he was acting.

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:17.067
-You all lived in the town?
-But I lived in the barbershop.

00:07:17.067 --> 00:07:18.934
And, so, every day, like,
the saloon doors

00:07:18.934 --> 00:07:20.133
would just be calling my name.

00:07:20.133 --> 00:07:22.000
Every day, I'd wake up
and I'd be like...

00:07:24.267 --> 00:07:25.534
"Good morning!"

00:07:25.534 --> 00:07:28.734
And everyone was like,
"God, five days in a row."

00:07:28.734 --> 00:07:30.567
-That's a --
Weirdly, I don't know why,

00:07:30.567 --> 00:07:32.000
but it's always been kind of
a dream of mine

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:33.000
to kick open a door.

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:34.167
-It's great.

00:07:34.167 --> 00:07:36.667
It's not fun when you do it
16 days in a row.

00:07:36.667 --> 00:07:38.534
-Yeah, but I don't know.
-For me, it was.

00:07:38.534 --> 00:07:40.934
-But look at how cool --
You're much cooler than I am.

00:07:40.934 --> 00:07:42.534
But, I mean,
I remember, in college,

00:07:42.534 --> 00:07:45.734
I had a playlist of songs that

00:07:45.734 --> 00:07:47.200
would be great
to kick doors open to.

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:48.200
-Cool.

00:07:48.200 --> 00:07:50.834
-Yeah, and Number 1 was

00:07:50.834 --> 00:07:52.868
"Misty Mountain Hop,"
Led Zeppelin.

00:07:52.868 --> 00:07:54.667
It goes like...
[ Vocalizing ]

00:07:58.267 --> 00:08:00.200
I'm like,
"Maybe what I'll do is,

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:01.968
I'll have someone
go into a bar,

00:08:01.968 --> 00:08:03.434
play that on the jukebox,

00:08:03.434 --> 00:08:05.067
and when it gets to
the right moment,

00:08:05.067 --> 00:08:06.133
I go...

00:08:06.133 --> 00:08:07.734
♪♪

00:08:07.734 --> 00:08:09.801
And just, "What's up, man?!"
You know?

00:08:09.801 --> 00:08:11.434
You go, "Oh, my gosh."

00:08:11.434 --> 00:08:14.701
I never got to live that.
-Well, I know the place.

00:08:14.701 --> 00:08:15.734
-The saloon?
-Yeah, I know the place.

00:08:15.734 --> 00:08:16.901
We'll go one day.

00:08:16.901 --> 00:08:18.167
-Alright, you tell me the bar,
and I'll go.

00:08:18.167 --> 00:08:19.467
-Yeah, we'll bring The Roots
so it can be as cool

00:08:19.467 --> 00:08:21.534
as what just happened.

00:08:21.534 --> 00:08:25.467
-Can you tell everyone --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:25.467 --> 00:08:27.968
Can you tell everyone
what the movie is about?

00:08:27.968 --> 00:08:32.734
-Yeah, so, it's almost --
To me --

00:08:32.734 --> 00:08:35.133
I mean, I don't want to
speak for the director.

00:08:35.133 --> 00:08:36.434
He might be like,
"What are you doing?"

00:08:36.434 --> 00:08:38.067
But, to me, it was almost
like Cronus, like,

00:08:38.067 --> 00:08:40.501
the Greek mythology of
the father who eats his sons,

00:08:40.501 --> 00:08:44.067
who they --
He's told one of his sons

00:08:44.067 --> 00:08:46.334
is going to overthrow him,
so he eats all of his kids

00:08:46.334 --> 00:08:47.400
so that they can't
overthrow him.

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:50.334
And it's the same thing
in this one.

00:08:50.334 --> 00:08:52.200
Like, Sam Worthington
is the father.

00:08:52.200 --> 00:08:54.701
He gets a curse where it's said

00:08:54.701 --> 00:08:57.067
that one of his kin
is going to kill him,

00:08:57.067 --> 00:08:59.267
so he goes
and he kills all of his kids.

00:08:59.267 --> 00:09:01.634
